{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrzvaWYvdz6YGAGZA9WH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `fetcher` package is now async, and all 7 tests pass (`python -m pytest -q`, 7 passed in 0.20s).\n\n- **`fetcher/client.py`**:\n  - `Client(transport=None, retries=3, backoff=0.01, max_concurrency=5)` now has `async get`, `async get_many`, `async close` and `async with` support.\n  - The default transport uses `asyncio.sleep`.\n  - Retries follow the same policy as before: exponential backoff, and only `TransientError` is retried.\n  - `get_many` runs requests concurrently, capped by a semaphore, and keeps input order. Per-URL errors come back as `FetchError` in the list.\n  - A closed client puts a `FetchError` in the result list instead of raising, as the sync version did.\n- **`fetcher/aggregate.py`**: `summarize` is `async` and returns the same shape.\n- **`fetcher/sync.py`** (new): `fetch_all(urls, transport=None)` runs the async client with `asyncio.run`.\n- **`tests/test_client.py`**:\n  - The three original tests are ported using plain `asyncio.run`, so there's no pytest-asyncio dependency.\n  - I added tests for retry exhaustion, no retry on non-transient errors, input order with the concurrency cap, a closed client, and `fetch_all`.\n\nOne addition you didn't ask for: the constructor raises `ValueError` if `max_concurrency` is below 1.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5259,"cache_read_input_tokens":33436,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5259},"output_tokens":500,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"771bfd8c-b958-44c7-88b6-b5ade77e6531","uuid":"23cd2f17-84a8-47e1-b919-625461209d3f","timesta